  "title": "Medical Canvassing vs. Records Retrieval vs. IME: Which Comes First and Why",
  "summary": "A canvass confirms whether and where treatment happened and needs no HIPAA release; records retrieval pulls the actual charts and requires a signed authorization; an IME adds an independent physician's opinion when causation is contested. Run them in that order — canvass, retrieve, then examine.",
